@startuml Logout Flow
skinparam style strictuml

actor Browser
participant "Gateway\n/auth/logout" as GW
database Redis
participant Keycloak

Browser -> GW: GET /api/v1/auth/logout\n(Cookie: gordle_session=abc123)
activate GW

== Destroy Server Session ==

GW -> Redis: Get("gordle:session:abc123")
Redis --> GW: session {id_token, refresh_token, ...}

GW -> Keycloak: POST /token\n(revoke refresh_token)
Keycloak --> GW: OK

GW -> Redis: Delete("gordle:session:abc123")
Redis --> GW: OK

== Clear Cookie ==

GW -> GW: Set-Cookie: gordle_session=""\nMaxAge=-1, HttpOnly

== Redirect to Keycloak Logout ==

GW -> GW: Build logout URL\nid_token_hint, client_id,\npost_logout_redirect_uri

Browser <-- GW: 302 Redirect → Keycloak /logout?id_token_hint=...
deactivate GW

Browser -> Keycloak: GET /realms/{realm}/protocol/openid-connect/logout?...
activate Keycloak

note right of Keycloak: id_token_hint allows\nKeycloak to skip\n"Do you want to log out?" page

Keycloak -> Keycloak: Destroy SSO session
Browser <-- Keycloak: 302 Redirect → http://localhost:3000
deactivate Keycloak

@enduml
